[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   Step 109 -- discovery-bias audit of the CometEls census dipole.
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   Step 108 found the full CometEls near-parabolic census (n=266)
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   leans toward the cap-declaration axis at d_par=+0.11 under a
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   galactic-tide-aware null.  The n=266 census is far more
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   heterogeneous than the three-leg elite samples -- it mixes
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   photographic-era and survey-era discoveries, bright and faint
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   comets, shallow and deep perihelia -- so the sharpest remaining
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   conventional explanation is discovery selection: comets are
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   catalogued preferentially through discovery windows organized in
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   ECLIPTIC coordinates (surveys scan the ecliptic plane), whereas
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   the tide-aware null is organized in GALACTIC coordinates.  This
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   step audits the census dipole against that hypothesis directly.
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   T1  ecliptic-footprint null: the dipole statistic re-evaluated
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   under a null that preserves the observed |beta_ecl| of each
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   aphelion while isotropizing ecliptic longitude and hemisphere
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   sign -- the survey-footprint-aware analogue of the step-061
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   tide null.  If the dipole were a discovery-window artefact
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   this is the null it should fail.
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   T2  magnitude stability: d_par in the bright and faint halves
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   and in H-terciles of the census.  Discovery selection is
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   magnitude-dependent; a selection artefact should scale with
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   H, a spatial structure should not.
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   T3  era stability: d_par in perihelion-year terciles -- the
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   photographic, early-CCD, and survey-era catalogues carry
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   different footprints.
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   T4  perihelion-distance stability: d_par in q-terciles --
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   shallow-perihelion comets are discovered at larger distances
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   and through different windows.
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   T5  heterogeneity summary: chi-square test of a single common
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   d_par across each variable's bins -- the formal test that
[2026-09-20 12:20:48 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 109]   the lean is a population property, not a subsample artefact.
